# MIGRATION RULES

Every schema modification MUST be a versioned migration.

NEVER:
- directly modify production;
- edit an applied migration;
- silently drop data;
- silently rename data-bearing columns/tables;
- bypass migration testing.

Before writing:
- inspect current schema;
- inspect migration history;
- inspect dependencies;
- inspect production-data impact;
- assess backward compatibility;
- assess API compatibility;
- assess index impact;
- define rollback/recovery.

Prefer backward-compatible changes.

Promote:
Local → Dev → Test → Staging → Production.

A failed migration blocks promotion.
